 "fill_reason": {
  "macro_channel": "37 macros (24 SRAM 128x256 in 3 banks x 2 columns x 4 rows, 7 ROM 4096x72 + 6 exponent SRAM 128x64 alternating in one S row) with 23.7 um row / 34.8 um column channels, 21.6-22 um ROM / exponent gaps; outline height 518.4 for routing room (the xs3 predecessor stalled in GRT congestion at 46 % utilisation); g_d enters the N face in [49.68, 583.2], the span of the ring stop leaf's S-face g_d."
 },
 "structural_change": "S81-XG4XS (LEAD4-S81 10-20): native-bounded successor of the S81-XG3 x streamer leaf ot_s81sl_xs3 (= ot_s81sl_xs RD2=2; mapped native census FAIL 1,156 drivers > 32, max 2,529: g_fam pin flops, mw_m write masks 1,024 macro pins, merged AND/NAND selects, rotation / read-bank / gather selects 256-435, gi_q 493, dq_r 490, cal reader rp 398, wpar 396/287, ctl reset 548, bc_hr 536; its --cts gate placed at -4.03 ns reg->macro (w_mask_in) / -4.01 ns reg->reg (tq_s) and stalled in GRT congestion iterations at 46 % util). Rebuilt from CURRENT MAIN ot_s81sl_xs as ot_s81sl_xs4 = main x streamer with one capture edge in front (K = 1): 21 kept capture copies per gather control port bit (v / fam / idx per source), one data flop per g_d / is_d bit, 2 is_v copies; level-B = main's pin flops in decoded form: 24 write leaves (8 x 9 kept one-hot data selects of 32 pins, 4 + 4 mask-half copies of 32 pins, w_ce / w_addr, own wpar replicas), arrival-table set one-hots per source in 16-beat blocks, 22 table groups of 8 beats with own parity replica / window clear, block exponents moved from a 3.84 kb flop array to 6 SRAMs (ot_sram_1r1w2c_128x64_m1, per source x beat bit 2); issuer delay line with registered one-hot write enables and 5 one-hot read-pointer copies (own pop compare each), 8 window-open copies; read side from 5 + 1 stream-head copies in the controller, arrival-table lookups by registered factorised one-hot indices, registered one-hot read-mux lines (12 / 24 per 32-b slice) into stage-3 AND-OR; stream-ROM bank one-hot copies; native calendar reader copy (one-hot row pointers, 6 due copies with own pointer / age / active, registered row write enables); native ctl copy (config-tag one-hot, hold-in-reset payload on regional enables, 36 bv copies for the lane word select); lane = dsfd_pq_lx STATIC_X2 function; reset port -> 2 sync -> 4 early / 54 / 4-stage 39 regions, every region <= 26 loads, payload reset-free. xs4_equiv (tools/s81_slice/xs4_equiv.sh, Verilator 5.050): vs main ot_s81sl_xs + one-edge tb relay on every input, xw_v / xw_d / fault every edge: 7 production L0 / L2 programs (near / far / rand ring orders, offsets 29-61), 2 late-beat programs (fault on the same edge), 10 fault injections (duplicate / out-of-range beats, reserved / offset / random issuer words, random gather bursts), 2 in-flight resets with program restart; 6 mutants (bank / off / qswap / wcopy / tpar / exp) FAIL. SAFE checklist (owner 10-19): 1 pins waived-with-reason (source-registered: every input lands in a capture flop, every output leaves the xw_q relay / fault flop; reset_landing 2 stages ON). 2 reach PASS by structure (capture -> level B -> macro / table: two hops across the 864-wide tile; read lines -> stage-3 output registers -> lane -> relay), checked by the placed gate. 3 fanout fixed by construction (<= 32 incl. resets and macro data / mask pins), checked by the gate's mandatory mapped native census. 4 depth PASS: one-hot AND-OR muxes, factorised lookups (~10 levels). 5 storage fixed: x buffer 24 SRAM, block exponents 6 SRAM (were 3.84 kb flops), arrival tables 1.06 kb flops in 22 groups, delay line 0.49 kb, calendar rows 0.4 kb. 6 floorplan: macros on the 21.6/43.2 lattice, 34.8 um column channels for the 10 pins/um SRAM L/R faces, ROM and exponent SRAMs alternating in the S row with 21.6-22 um gaps, full-width std band N (capture) and between banks; outline from routing room (xs3 congested at 46 %): see variant. 7 clock: clock_split_km regional roots K=16, spread judged TT+FF <= 80; io_hold_margin 0.03. 8 schedule: +1 edge on the whole x streamer (gather and issuer alike; equal on xw_v / xw_d / fault) vs main ot_s81sl_xs -> MU.S81.CAL prices it; with the rs4 RELAY = 1 gather edge a gathered beat lands 2 edges and an issuer word 1 edge later than in main ot_s81sl_xg; static schedule, no ready / credit. Variant b: 864 x 518.4 (util ~42 %, row channels 23.7 um).",
